          {
            "type": "break"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "value": "Traffic going from Corp-A-DC-2 towards Corp-B will always use Link-1. Traffic from Corp-B back to Corp-A-DC-1 may traverse Corp-A-DC-1, over the GigaMAN before it reaches Corp-A-DC-2. No TCP connections are initiated from Corp-B to either Corp-A-DC-1 or Corp-A-DC-2. Unfortunately, the customer does not have any money to purchase any additional Steelheads. What are some possible fixes to ensure optimization occurs while Link-1 is operational? (If Link-1 ceases to function, optimization is not possible.) (Select 2)"
          }
        ]
      },
      "Choices": {
        "A": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "A. Configure a fixed-target rule on the Corp-A-DC-2 Steelhead pointing to the Corp-B Steelhead on port 7800"
            }
          ]
        },
        "B": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "B. On the Corp-B Steelhead, enable \"in-path probe direct\""
            }
          ]
        },
        "C": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "C. On the Corp-A-DC-2 Steelhead, enable \"in-path probe direct\""
            }
          ]
        },
        "D": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "D. Configure the Corp-A-DC-2 Steelhead to inject a route into the network"
            }
          ]
        },
        "E": {
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "E. Enable Full Transparency"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "Answer": {
        "content": []
      },
